Maintainer: Vincent Runge <vincent.runge@univ-evry.fr>
Description: We segment a univariate time series using the Smallest Valid Partition algorithm. 
    The method is a new change-point detection approach that enforces local segment quality through a validity test. 
    A segment is declared valid if it passes the test; otherwise (i.e., if a change-point is detected) it is invalid and excluded from the final segmentation.
